se Products\". The scenario says the visitor follows \"Browse Products\", so the test would still pass if the label were renamed to anything. The page does say \"Browse Products\" today (`index.pug:11`), but no test checks it.\n\nThe fix is one assertion on the label, the same way the View Cart (`:175`) and Shop Now (`:242`) tests already check theirs. The test also needs a new break patch that renames the label.\n\n**The other six scenarios are proved.** Each test sets up the starting point, does the action and checks every expected result with the story's exact values.\n\n**Not treated as defects:**\n- The integration tests read the rendered HTML rather than driving a browser. That is correct here: only the main scenario needs a browser test, and it has one.\n- The Shop Now test checks that the link is in the same section as the heading and the sentence, not strictly below them. I counted that as a fair reading of \"below\", minor at most.\n\nOf the review perspectives, the added `dca` review didn't run, because there was no production code to review. I didn't consult `dca-knowledge`, since no architecture question came up. No other stage was run.","ttft_ms":2977,"type":"result","duration_ms":64642,"uuid":"ffbfce1f-96c9-40fb-be5a-3852a1fd5017","ttft_stream_ms":1596,"time_to_request_ms":35,"first_content_frame_ms":1596,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
